hing is converted to SI units before it goes into the equations.", "latex": [], "substeps": [], "table": {"headers": ["\\text{quantity}", "\\text{symbol}", "\\text{given}", "\\text{SI}"], "rows": [["\\text{Surrounding temperature}", "T_\\infty", "22\\ \\mathrm{^\\circ C}", "295.1\\ \\mathrm{K}"], ["\\text{Initial temperature}", "T_0", "90\\ \\mathrm{^\\circ C}", "363.1\\ \\mathrm{K}"], ["\\text{Time}", "t", "5\\ \\mathrm{min}", "300\\ \\mathrm{s}"], ["\\text{Temperature at that time}", "T", "75\\ \\mathrm{^\\circ C}", "348.1\\ \\mathrm{K}"], ["\\text{Temperature at the second time}", "T_2", "60\\ \\mathrm{^\\circ C}", "333.1\\ \\mathrm{K}"]]}}, {"title": "Find the fraction of the initial difference left (growth: growth factor)", "text": "The value at time t is where it is heading plus what is left of the initial difference. With \\(T = 75\\ \\mathrm{^\\circ C}\\), \\(T_0 = 90\\ \\mathrm{^\\circ C}\\), \\(T_\\infty = 22\\ \\mathrm{^\\circ C}\\).", "latex": ["f = \\frac{T - T_\\infty}{T_0 - T_\\infty}", "f = 0.7794"], "substeps": []}, {"title": "Find the rate constant", "text": "The difference from where it is heading shrinks exponentially. With \\(f = 0.7794\\), \\(t = 5\\ \\mathrm{min}\\).", "latex": ["k = -\\frac{\\ln f}{t}", "k = 0.04984\\ \\mathrm{min^{-1}}"], "substeps": []}, {"title": "Find the time constant", "text": "The time constant is the reciprocal of the rate constant. With \\(k = 0.04984\\ \\mathrm{min^{-1}}\\).", "latex": ["\\tau = \\frac{1}{k}", "\\tau = 1204\\ \\mathrm{s}"], "substeps": []}, {"title": "Find the half-life (growth: doubling time)", "text": "The time for the difference to halve. With \\(k = 0.04984\\ \\mathrm{min^{-1}}\\).", "latex": ["t_{1/2} = \\frac{\\ln 2}{k}", "t_{1/2} = 834.4\\ \\mathrm{s}"], "substeps": []}, {"title": "Find the second time", "text": "The same solution read at the second time. With \\(T_2 = 60\\ \\mathrm{^\\circ C}\\), \\(T_0 = 90\\ \\mathrm{^\\circ C}\\), \\(k = 0.04984\\ \\mathrm{min^{-1}}\\), \\(T_\\infty = 22\